From 826992888ba1b32f762b6c26f2354c6f87d56a6a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: blank <583957236@qq.com>
Date: Wed, 1 Apr 2026 13:56:35 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/8] feat(def): add keyword lookup implementation selection
 with gperf optimization

Add macro-controlled keyword lookup implementations for performance comparison:
- DEF_KEYWORD_GPERF (default): Use gperf perfect hash, O(1) guaranteed
- DEF_KEYWORD_STD_MAP: Use std::map, O(log n)
- DEF_KEYWORD_UNORDERED_MAP: Use std::unordered_map with string_view, O(1) average

Changes:
- def_keywords.cpp: Add implementation selection via macros
- defrSettings.hpp: Add typedef for different map types
- template.mk: Add KEYWORD_IMPL parameter for build selection
- defrData.cpp/hpp: Add buffer capacity tracking for realloc optimization

Performance test results (10 runs, 462MB Galaxy.def):
- GPERF: 5.18s (-nc), 6.60s (full)
- UNORDERED_MAP: 6.00s (-nc), 7.48s (full)
- STD_MAP: 6.08s (-nc), 7.78s (full)

GPERF remains the optimal implementation for keyword lookup.

Build: make release KEYWORD_IMPL=[gperf|std_map|unordered_map]
